d  darlin had just touched her daughter's  fingers when she felt mr. scales  powerful arm encircling her waist she  screamed but the sound was pitiful  carried away by the strange cold breeze  don't fight woman the voice croaked in  her head your end will be quit no darlin  struggled hard filling the creature's  sandpaper skin against her cheek and  neck she threw her head back seeing the  lights from inside the shadowed forms  moving behind the French doors  Warren was there he must be missing them  by now surely he would come out soon to  see where they had gone no one will come  for you mr. scales whispered into her  brain as though he was reading her  thoughts your daughter is blameless so  she will be spared to live with me  forever and my beautiful small but you  he made a strange bellowing sound a  sound of disgust no one knew what you  wished about your parents but I knew  Darlene began hitting him in the chest  with her fists but it felt like he was  wearing armor why did you grant my wish  then she shrieked why you asked I do he  croaked simply it is my purse with that  the muscles in his arms tightened until  Darlene felt trapped by bands of iron  she tried to scream again but she could  get no air her lungs seemed filled with  swamp water green and black and muddy  her feet left the floor of the deck and  she was falling falling backwards then  there was a splash and it was cold so  very cold misty screamed and beat her  arms against the water but then even  that sound became muted as Darlene was  dragged under the water of the lake the  lake that led to the swamps the swamps  where she had been born the water  cradled her like a lover and mr. scales  wrapped his powerful arms around her  body and the world went silent and green  and then it went black
 

